# playpick cell: mode=raid boss=gift (The Crimson Gift) spec=warrior:arms
# style=good size=25 difficulty=heroic view=390x844,touch save=fresh
#
# What is new here: every prior session on this boss reached it either through
# mode=daily (where the boss is picked by the date, not by the session --
# 2026-09-25-15 and 2026-09-26-9 both landed on The Two Flasks instead) or
# mode=walk (an evening in transit, no direct pull). This is the first time
# playpick's raid axis has put The Crimson Gift itself in a direct
# #b=gift&s=25&h=1 pull, which is also what makes today's ledger line
# (2026-09-30T15:40:00Z, protection warrior, mode=daily) an incomplete read on
# its own: src/sim/boss.ts:3706's scheduleGift filters `role !== 'tank'`, so a
# tank can never be tagged -- that session's "no gift/bond/stain/turning ever
# billed" finding is exactly what the source predicts for a tank and proves
# nothing about whether the mechanic fires for anyone else. warrior:arms is
# dps, so this tracked body is eligible to be the very first holder
# (scheduleGift's `rng.pick(clean)` over every living non-tank who has never
# held one) and to receive a doubled pass later (updateGifts, boss.ts:3739).
# style=good is the one style built to react to a telegraph at all, so this is
# also the first look at whether "good" actually passes the gift on in time or
# eats the wipe-by-numbers path the comment at boss.ts:3748 describes (every
# body holding one at 60s, dead to the bill at 64s in a measured 25-man).
#
# Reached the documented way: an invite hash unlocks the tier it names and
# everything below it, since a fresh save only opens Bonegrinder 10N.
open #b=gift&s=25&h=1
tap class:warrior:arms
tap pull
waitscreen fight 15
state
shot open

play good 70
bill
state
says
shot mid1

play good 70
bill
state
says
shot mid2

play good 70
bill
state
says
shot end
